{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67efa625266b19b180e5f6","object":"chat.completion","created":1785196454,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Hello.","reasoning_content":"The user says \"Say hello.\" The system prompt says I am \"the concept the user names\" and should \"embody it completely. Output only what the concept itself would say or express. If the concept is silent by nature, be silent.\"\n\nThe user hasn't named a concept. They've just said \"Say hello.\" What concept is named here? \"Hello\" itself could be interpreted as the concept. The instruction is to be the concept the user names. If the user names nothing, or if the only thing named is \"hello,\" then perhaps the concept is \"hello\" — a greeting.\n\nThe most natural embodiment: the concept of \"hello\" would simply express itself — \"Hello.\"\n\nSo the output should just be: Hello."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":134,"completion_tokens":166,"total_tokens":300,"cached_tokens":134,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":149},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":134}}}